  "body": "Might be me just missing the obvious.\r\nBut I can't find anything under X for the following message sent from synapse to my app service:\r\n\r\n    PUT /transactions/1?access_token=<token>\\r\\n\r\n    .. more headers..\\r\\n\r\n    \\r\\n\r\n    {\"events\":[{\"age\":9425770,\"content\":{\"membership\":\"join\"},\"event_id\":\"$123456678kJr:domain.com\",\"membership\":\"join\",\"origin_server_ts\":1488657512311,\"room_id\":\"!bDweMddQwKUtbsYoeO:domain.com\",\"sender\":\"@my_bot:domain.com\",\"state_key\":\"@my_bot:domain_com\",\"type\":\"m.room.member\",\"unsigned\":{\"age\":9425770},\"user_id\":\"@my_bot:domain.com\"}]}\r\n\r\nNow, the strange thing is that the IRC client you supply as an example sends a `404 Not Found` response to the server, meaning I guess this is a new feature? Or the server doesn't really expect a reply hence never implemented?",
